module engine where

-- derive-foldable — the generic, schema-directed `foldr` (the Foldable half of
-- the kinds-arc derivation, unified-static-analysis Phase 6c).
--
-- Any `* -> *` type WITHOUT an authored `Foldable` instance gets `foldr` for
-- FREE: a single always-on structural `Foldable` instance keyed by
-- `{$pattern:"engine:isUnaryConstructor"}` resolves through the SHIPPED
-- `matchStructural` substrate, and its `foldr` is `engine:deriveFoldr` — a thin
-- category-B reflection+marshal bridge (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts) that resolves
-- the dispatched value's owning type, marshals its schema across the `$`-key
-- barrier via `marshalTraversalType`, and delegates the DECISION to THIS body.
-- The authored `Maybe`/`List`/`Result` instances keep nominal precedence
-- (`resolveStructural` is the last fall-through), so this only fires for
-- previously-uninstanced unary constructors (e.g. a user `Box a` / `Tree a`).
--
-- This is the `$tag`-correct, multi-param-SOUND Fenel successor to the stale
-- `__case`-era TS `structuralFold` (engine/src/structural.ts): it classifies
-- fields by the FUNCTOR-PARAM IDENTITY (`TtVar paramName`), recurses on
-- self-recursive fields (`TtNamed typeName`), RE-DISPATCHES one-level nested
-- foreign functors (`TtApp` whose args carry the param — D-6c closes the
-- D-6b-5 fence), and SKIPS every other field — where `structuralFold` folded
-- EVERY non-recursive field (wrong for `Result`'s `e`, `Pair2 e a`'s `e`, …).
--
-- RIGHT-FOLD ORDER. `foldr f z [x0,x1,x2] = f x0 (f x1 (f x2 z))` — the
-- rightmost element touches the seed first. `deriveFoldrFields` recurses the
-- TAIL first (building the folded-rest accumulator), then combines the HEAD
-- field on top, so multi-field cases fold last-to-first (mirroring the `foldr`
-- contract + `structuralFold`'s field order).
--
-- TOTALITY (D-6c-5 / D-6b-4): the recursion descends ONLY into self-recursive
-- sub-values (`fieldVal` is a structural sub-term of `value`), strictly smaller
-- each step; an unknown tag / non-record value / unrecognised field-type ⇒
-- return the seed (never crash). The fold is its own dog-food for the totality
-- checker this workstream builds.
--
-- FENCE (D-6c-2): COMPOUND nesting where the param sits TWO functors deep
-- (`List (Box a)` ⇒ the inner `TtApp` arg is itself a `TtApp`, not a bare
-- `TtVar paramName`) needs `foldr (foldr ..)` composition — NOT closed by v1;
-- such a field is SKIPPED (treated like any non-param field), documented here,
-- never silently mis-folded. The common cases (`List a`, `Maybe a` fields) ARE
-- closed by the one-level re-dispatch.
--
-- `$map`-FIELD DESCENT (D-6c-3 CLOSED, array-substrate Phase 1a). A `TtMap` field
-- whose VALUES carry the functor param (`Map String a`) is FOLDED by `mapFoldr f
-- acc` over the field value — the `Foldable (Map k)` operation (folds the map's
-- values into the threaded accumulator). A direct call, NOT a `Foldable.foldr`
-- re-dispatch (a bare map field has no `$tag` to dispatch on — the Phase-1a
-- Step-0 fact). COMPOUND map values (`Map String (Box a)`) stay SKIPPED (D-6c-2).
--
-- The continuation `f` is the BINARY binop closure-valued PARAM; applying it to
-- two args is `(f $ elem) $ acc` — `$` (`($) f x = f x`) is right-associative,
-- so the explicit parens force left-application (`f $ elem` curries to `b -> b`,
-- then `$ acc` applies). std fns (`mapGet`/`eq`/`head`/`tail`) are called by
-- bare codeName (the engine-body idiom). All helpers are prefixed
-- `deriveFoldr…` to avoid registry collisions with derive-functor.fenel's
-- `deriveFmap…` family.

-- deriveFoldrFold — the entry. `f` the binop, `seed` the fold seed, `value` the
-- runtime functor value, `schemaView` the dispatched type's schema marshalled to
-- TraversalType, `paramName` the functor type-param name (the type's LAST
-- declared param), `typeName` the owning type-constructor name (for
-- self-recursion detection). Peels the schema wrappers to the variant/record,
-- finds the matching case, folds its fields. The `typeName` arg mirrors
-- `deriveFmapFold`'s build-time amendment — self-recursion is `TtNamed typeName`.
@label "Derive foldr (generic fold)"
@description "Phase 6c — the generic schema-directed `foldr`: any `* -> *` type without an authored Foldable instance gets foldr free. Folds the functor-param leaves (TtVar paramName) into the seed with the binop, recurses self-recursive fields (TtNamed typeName), re-dispatches one-level nested foreign functors (TtApp carrying the param), skips the rest (multi-param sound, the structuralFold repair). The decision half of the derived Foldable instance; the engine:deriveFoldr bridge supplies (f, seed, value, schemaView, paramName, typeName). Right-fold order; total: descends only into strictly-smaller self-recursive sub-values."
@tags "engine" "foldable" "derive" "kinds" "phase-6c"
deriveFoldrFold : (f: a) -> (seed: b) -> (value: c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFoldrFold f seed value schemaView paramName typeName =
  case schemaView of
    TtOpaque { pure = p } -> deriveFoldrFold f seed value p paramName typeName
    TtRefined { base = bse } -> deriveFoldrFold f seed value bse paramName typeName
    TtMu { body = bdy } -> deriveFoldrFold f seed value bdy paramName typeName
    TtRecord { fields = fs } ->
      deriveFoldrFields f seed value fs schemaView paramName typeName
    TtVariant { cases = cs } ->
      case mapGet value "$tag" of
        Nothing -> seed
        Just tag ->
          case deriveFoldrFindCase cs tag of
            Nothing -> seed
            Just c -> deriveFoldrFields f seed value c.fields schemaView paramName typeName
    _ -> seed

-- deriveFoldrFindCase — locate the variant case whose name matches the value's
-- `$tag`. Internal helper; head/tail recursion (the array-repr List idiom).
@label "derive-foldable: findCase"
@description "Phase 6c — locate the TtVariantCase matching the value's $tag. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "foldable" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFoldrFindCase : (cases: List a) -> (tag: String) -> Maybe a
deriveFoldrFindCase cases tag =
  case head cases of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just c ->
      if eq c.name tag
        then Just c
        else case tail cases of
          Nothing -> Nothing
          Just rest -> deriveFoldrFindCase rest tag

-- deriveFoldrFields — the RIGHT-fold over a case's declared fields. Recurse the
-- TAIL first (the folded-rest accumulator), then combine the HEAD field on top,
-- so fields fold last-to-first (the foldr contract). Internal helper.
@label "derive-foldable: foldFields"
@description "Phase 6c — right-fold over a case's declared fields: recurse the tail to a folded-rest accumulator, then step the head field on top (last-to-first). Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "foldable" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFoldrFields : (f: a) -> (seed: b) -> (value: c) -> (fields: List d) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFoldrFields f seed value fields schemaView paramName typeName =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> seed
    Just fld ->
      case tail fields of
        Nothing ->
          deriveFoldrStepField f seed value fld schemaView paramName typeName
        Just rest ->
          let restAcc = deriveFoldrFields f seed value rest schemaView paramName typeName
          deriveFoldrStepField f restAcc value fld schemaView paramName typeName

-- deriveFoldrStepField — one field step. A field absent from the value (a partial
-- record) leaves the accumulator untouched; else classify+fold it. Split out to
-- avoid a `case`-in-`let` (the analyze.fenel/totality.fenel idiom).
@label "derive-foldable: stepField"
@description "Phase 6c — one field: read the value's field (absent ⇒ leave acc untouched), classify+fold onto acc. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "foldable" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFoldrStepField : (f: a) -> (acc: b) -> (value: c) -> (fld: d) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFoldrStepField f acc value fld schemaView paramName typeName =
  case mapGet value fld.name of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just fieldVal ->
      deriveFoldrFoldField f acc fieldVal fld.type schemaView paramName typeName

-- deriveFoldrFoldField — CLASSIFY one field by its marshalled TraversalType:
--   element        — `TtVar paramName`   ⇒ combine into acc with the binop.
--   self-recursive — `TtNamed typeName`  ⇒ recurse `deriveFoldrFold` (thread acc).
--   nested functor — `TtApp` whose args carry `TtVar paramName` ⇒ RE-DISPATCH
--                    `Foldable.foldr f acc fieldVal` (the nested functor folds
--                    its OWN elements with the same binop into the threaded
--                    accumulator — nominal for `List`/`Maybe`, derived for a
--                    user functor). D-6c closes the D-6b-5 fence (one level).
--   map-field      — `TtMap` whose values carry the param ⇒ `mapFoldr f acc` over
--                    the map's values (D-6c-3, closed Phase 1a — a direct call,
--                    the bare map field has no `$tag` to re-dispatch on).
--   otherwise (a different type-var `e`, a fixed `Int`, an unrelated named type,
--             a compound-nested `TtApp`/`TtMap`) ⇒ LEAVE acc unchanged.
-- D-6c-5: classification is by FUNCTOR-PARAM IDENTITY — the multi-param
-- soundness over the legacy `structuralFold`.
@label "derive-foldable: foldField"
@description "Phase 6c/1a — classify a field by its TraversalType: TtVar paramName ⇒ fold into acc (the functor param); TtNamed typeName ⇒ recurse (self-recursive); TtApp carrying the param ⇒ re-dispatch Foldable.foldr on the nested functor value (D-6b-5, one level); TtMap whose values carry the param ⇒ mapFoldr f acc over the map values (D-6c-3, closed Phase 1a); else leave (other vars / fixed types / compound nesting). Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "foldable" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFoldrFoldField : (f: a) -> (acc: b) -> (fieldVal: c) -> (ft: TraversalType) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFoldrFoldField f acc fieldVal ft schemaView paramName typeName =
  case ft of
    TtVar { name = vn } ->
      if eq vn paramName
        then (f $ fieldVal) $ acc
        else acc
    TtNamed { name = nn } ->
      if eq nn typeName
        then deriveFoldrFold f acc fieldVal schemaView paramName typeName
        else acc
    TtApp { args = as } ->
      if deriveFoldrAppHasParam as paramName
        then foldr f acc fieldVal
        else acc
    TtMap { values = vs } ->
      if deriveFoldrArgIsParam vs paramName
        then mapFoldr f acc fieldVal
        else acc
    _ -> acc

-- deriveFoldrAppHasParam — does this applied-type's arg list carry the functor
-- param DIRECTLY as one of its args (`Con .. a ..`)? Only a bare `TtVar
-- paramName` at the top of the arg list counts — a nested `TtApp` arg (compound
-- nesting, `List (Box a)`) does NOT, so it falls to the SKIP branch (D-6c-2
-- fence). Internal helper; head/tail recursion.
@label "derive-foldable: appHasParam"
@description "Phase 6c — does an applied-type's arg list carry the functor param directly (one-level nesting)? A nested TtApp arg (compound nesting) does NOT count — D-6c-2 fence. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "foldable" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFoldrAppHasParam : (args: List a) -> (paramName: String) -> Bool
deriveFoldrAppHasParam args paramName =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> false
    Just a ->
      if deriveFoldrArgIsParam a paramName
        then true
        else case tail args of
          Nothing -> false
          Just rest -> deriveFoldrAppHasParam rest paramName

-- deriveFoldrArgIsParam — is this single TraversalType arg the functor param
-- (`TtVar paramName`)? Internal helper.
@label "derive-foldable: argIsParam"
@description "Phase 6c — is a single TraversalType arg the functor param (TtVar paramName)? Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "foldable" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFoldrArgIsParam : (a: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> Bool
deriveFoldrArgIsParam a paramName =
  case a of
    TtVar { name = vn } -> eq vn paramName
    _ -> false
